  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\n## COLLEGE CONTACTS Years 7-12\n\nTelephone:   9208 2500 Facsimile: 9271 9663 Uniform Shop: 9208 2690 Canteen: 9208 2565 WWW .chisholm.wa.edu.au admin@chisholm.wa.edu\\_\n\nau\n\nOffice Hours: 8.15am 4.30pm P 0 Box 89 Inglewood\n\n6932\n\n## OUR WEEKEND PARISH MASSES\n\nMacKillop Catholic ComMary\n\n## BALLAJURA\n\nmunity\n\nSunday 8am, 9.30am &amp; 5pm\n\nSaturday 6pm,\n\n## BASSENDEAN\n\n## ST JOSEPH'S\n\nSaturday 6.3Opm Sunday 7am &amp; 9am\n\n## BAYSWATER\n\nSaturday 6pm\n\nSt Columba's\n\nSunday 7.3Oam &amp; 9.30am\n\nmonth 6pm\n\nYouth: Last Saturday of the\n\nBEDFORD\n\nSt Peter's\n\n&amp; 1Oam\n\nSaturday 6pm, Sunday 8.30am\n\n## DIANELLA\n\nSunday 7.3Oam &amp; 9.30am\n\nOur Lady's Assumption Saturday 6.3Opm\n\n## EMBLETON\n\nSaturday 6pm, Sunday 9am\n\nHoly Trinity\n\nAboriginal Mass at 11am\n\nSacred Heart\n\n## HIGHGATE\n\nSaturday 6pm\n\n## LOCKRIDGE\n\nSunday 9am &amp; 10.15am (Italian)\n\nGood Shepherd\n\nSunday 8am, 9.30am &amp; 5pm\n\nSaturday 6.3Opm\n\n## MAYLANDS\n\nQueen of Martyrs\n\n&amp; 7pm\n\nSaturday 6pm, Sunday 9.3Oam\n\n## MORLEY\n\nInfant Jesus Saturday 6.3Opm 11.3Oam (Italian) &amp; 6pm Youth: 2nd &amp; 4th Sundays 6pm\n\n## CANTEEN ROSTER FOR WEEK COMMENCING Monday 25th October 2010\n\n| Mon 25th              | Tue 26th                | Wed 27th               | Thu 28th            | Fri 29th                                      |\n|-----------------------|-------------------------|------------------------|---------------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| M White 9.15am-1.3Opm | S Washbourne 9am-1.3Opm | C Smith 8.30am-11.30am | L Pinner 9am-1.3Opm | D Audino 8.30am-1lam R Nocciolino 10.30am-2pm |\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nOn Monday 18th October; approximately 500 members of our Chisholm community gathered to acknowledge some of the wonderful team and individual sporting performances for 2010.  Special guests Ms Shae Bolton West Coast Fever Netball) and\n\nMr Trent Mitton (Kookaburras medalist at the recent Delhi Commonwealth Games) shared the night with our future sporting stars. Both were able to offer some advice and inspiration for all who attended. gold\n\nTrent with Lara Ameduri and Danika Vidakovich\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nCongratulations to all our award winners and in particular\n\nJustin Skowron who was awarded the  Peter Tonkin? award for the most outstanding Year 12 sports person.\n\nWell done to all of you.\n\nMr Andrew Glover, Head of Sport\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n## STUDENT CONGRATULATIONS William Edge Year IILaurencel\n\nWilliam has been selected to represent WA in the upcoming All Australian Basketball Tour to USA. He will participate in several competitions on the West Coast of America and play against some of the best USA College Basketball Teams: The tour takes in LA, San Las Vegas and Phoenix and will last from 28th Nov to 23d Dec: Well done William and good luck for the Tour. We are very proud of you: Diego,\n\n## HAVE YOUR SAY ON PUBLIC TRANSPORT IN YOUR LOCAL COMMUNITY ADVANCING PERTHS EASTERN REGION\n\nSeven Public Transport Forums are being held across the region during October and November 2010. These forums aim to engage and encourage the community to become more aware of the vision for increased transport and the options and delivery modes that exist. You can register by contacting Samantha Robshaw on email samantha robshaw@emrc org au public",
